node_modules/
out/
dist/
release/
*.log
.DS_Store
.vite/
.env
.env.local

# TypeScript incremental build state, not source.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Stray backup files left by patch tools.
*.orig

# graphify's generated knowledge graph: regenerated by `graphify update .`,
# and graph.json alone can run to tens of thousands of lines — committing it
# would put a multi-megabyte generated artifact in front of every diff and
# every reviewer. Keep it locally, never in git.
graphify-out/

# Isolated worktrees and subagent-driven-development scratch. Both are local
# working state, not source: committing a worktree would put the whole tree
# in the repo a second time, and the SDD ledger is a recovery map for one
# session, not a record anyone reads later.
# Local Claude Code configuration and scratch. settings.json accumulates
# machine-specific permission grants with absolute home paths in them, and a
# worktree committed to the repository would put the whole tree in twice.
# Local tooling state, never source.
.claude/
.superpowers/
